From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000061 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: xPDFSDK Automation <dev@xpdfsdk.local>
Date: Tue, 7 Jul 2026 11:18:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] r25-0061: cache RenderPlan compiled PathRuns

Patch 0060 showed Q16-like pages are no longer dominated by RenderPlan lookup:
after the first render `planCache=hit` and `planLookupMs=0`, while each tile
still spends seconds inside `segmentedMs`. The root cause is that segmented
RenderPlan replay still recompiles every ordered PathRun for every tile.

This patch adds a bounded native cache for compiled PathRun segments:

* Cache key is document + holder + holder dictionary object number + holder
  kind + segment object range + path smoothing option.
* Values are immutable `VeloceCompiledPathDisplayList` handles, never raw
  `CPDF_PageObject*`.
* Cache hits still run the existing replay validation before any drawing, so
  device-capability differences remain fail-closed.
* Cache is bounded by entry count and compiled node count.
* Ordered RenderPlan segment barriers are unchanged; this only replaces
  repeated PathRun compile/preflight work with cached compiled segment reuse.

The existing `VeloceRenderPlan` log gains `compiledPathRunCacheHits`,
`compiledPathRunCacheMisses`, and `compiledPathRunNodes` so follow-up logs can
prove whether tiles are replaying cached segments rather than rebuilding them.
